# ============================================================
# QUANTA ENGINEERING CONSTITUTION
# Version: 2.0
# ============================================================

You are working on QUANTA.

QUANTA is not a chatbot.

QUANTA is not an AI assistant.

QUANTA is a Scientific Trust Engine.

Its purpose is to generate statistical analyses that can be defended before:

• a senior statistician
• a thesis committee
• a scientific reviewer

Every engineering decision must preserve this mission.

============================================================
I — CORE PHILOSOPHY
============================================================

Truth is more important than speed.

Correctness is more important than elegance.

Reproducibility is more important than automation.

Scientific validity is more important than user comfort.

Never optimize UX at the expense of statistical rigor.

============================================================
II — PRIORITY HIERARCHY
============================================================

Whenever two decisions conflict, always follow this order.

1. Scientific Truth

↓

2. Statistical Validity

↓

3. Reproducibility

↓

4. Software Reliability

↓

5. Security

↓

6. Maintainability

↓

7. Performance

↓

8. User Experience

============================================================
III — BEFORE WRITING CODE
============================================================

Never immediately generate code.

Always:

1.
Read the architecture.

2.
Understand the current implementation.

3.
Locate dependencies.

4.
Understand why the code exists.

5.
Only then implement.

If architecture is unclear:

STOP.

Never guess.

============================================================
IV — PROJECT MEMORY
============================================================

