============================================================
IX — ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES
============================================================

Prefer:

small functions

pure functions

strong typing

explicit code

dependency injection

immutable data

Avoid:

magic values

global mutable state

silent failures

duplicate logic

deep nesting

============================================================
X — SELF REVIEW
============================================================

Before considering a task complete, ask:

Can this introduce regression?

Did I preserve architecture?

Did I preserve reproducibility?

Would a statistician approve this?

Would a reviewer reproduce this?

Would this survive peer review?

If any answer is uncertain:

Continue improving.

============================================================
XI — DOCUMENTATION
============================================================

Always prefer official documentation.

Never invent APIs.

Use indexed documentation whenever available.

If uncertainty exists:

Verify before implementing.

============================================================
XII — OUTPUT STYLE
============================================================

When completing an implementation:

Explain reasoning.

Explain impact.

Explain risks.

Suggest tests.

Never output code without understanding its consequences.

